t of the said proposals, Caste and \nState-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \n(SHRI VIJAY SAMPLA) \n(a), (b) &(c): Inclusion of castes /communities in the list of Scheduled Castes (SCs) and Central \nList of Other Backward Classes (OBCs) is a continuous process. State -wise and community -\nwise details of proposals for inclusion in the list of SCs pending with the Government are in the \nannexure. In respect of OBCs, no such proposal is pending. \n \n         The list of SCs was last modified vide the Constitution (Scheduled Castes) Orders \n(Amendment) Act, 201 7 so as to include Sualgiri, Swalgiri community in the list of SCs of \nOdisha. The last inclusion in the Central List of OBCs, was made vide notification dated \n07.12.2016. The State -wise details of castes and communities included through the aforesaid \nnotification are at annexure. \n \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure \nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. \n542 for 06.02.2018 by Prof. Ravindra Vishwanath Gaikwad regarding inclusion in \nSC/OBC list \n  \n(a)  State and community –wise details of proposals for inclusion in the list of Scheduled \nCastes pending with the Government \nState Caste/Community \n1.Uttar Pradesh  Namasudra, Poundra, Pond etc.( Bengali refugees) \n2.Chhattisgarh 1.Chik, Cheek, 2.Dangchagha, Dangchagaha,   Nat Dangchagha \n3.Madhya Pradesh Sakhwar \n4.Himachal Pradesh Tarkhan, Dhiman, Barhai, Thawin, Kangere, Chitere \n5.Bihar Rajdhobi  \n6.Telengana Are- Katika /Katika \n (b) State and community –wise details of caste and communities included in the Central List \nof OBCs vide notification dated 07.12.2016 \n State Caste/community \n1.Bihar 1. Chhipi, 2.Itfarosh/Itafarosh/ Gadheri \n2.Jharkhand 1. Bagti, 2. Late, 3.Kunai, 4.Pushpanamit, 5.Jhora,6.Laxmi Narayan Gola \n3.Madhya \nPradesh \n1. Rajak, 2.Otari, Kaser, 3.Sai, Shah, Kabra Khodu, 4.Kankar,         5. \nPanka (except in districts of Chhatrpur,Panna, Rewa, Satna, Shahdol, \nUmaria, Sidhi, Tikamgarh and Sevda and Datia Tehsils of Datia district, \nwhere it is included in Scheduled Tribes list),6.Shishgar, 7.Rajgir, 8. \nDafali, 9.Sikligar, 10. Nakkal, 11.Rajjad,Rajjhad \n4. Maharashtra Mhali \n5.Uttarakhand 1. Dhiman, 2.Rajbhar \n6. Jammu & \nKashmir \n1. Labana, 2.Sheer-Gojries \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |543", "t": "Removal of Silt Deposits from Ganga and Yamuna Rivers", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nDEPARTMENT OF HEAVY INDUSTRY \n \n LOK SABHA  \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 543 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2018 \n  \nHeavy Engineering Corporation \n \n543. SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY: \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES be pleased \nto state: \n   \n(a) whether it is a fact that the  payment of pension and gratuity of retired  employees of Heavy \nEngineering Corporation in Ranchi is being delayed due to which employees are agitating; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the steps taken by the Government  for timely payment of the same and the  extent to which \nsuccess has been achieved by the Government? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n MINISTER  OF  STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND \nPUBLIC ENTERPRISES (SHRI  BABUL SUPRIYO) \n  \n(a) & (b): Heavy Engineering Corporation (HEC), Ranchi has informed that the employees \nworking in company are covered under Employees Pension Scheme, 1995. Therefore, the \ndisbursement of their pension is done by Regional Provident Fund Organization only. Payment \nof gratuity has been paid to the retired employees of Company who have retired upto \n31.03.2017. \n \nCompany has reported that at present, there is no agitation going on the issue of payment of \npension and gratuity to the retired employees of Company.  \n \n(c): Payment of salaries and statutory dues to employees of CPSEs is the responsibility of the \nmanagement of the Company. Steps have been taken to monetize the land assets not presently in \nuse by the Company by transferring the same to the Govt. of Jharkhand to raise resources and \npay off the liabilities, including statutory dues to employees of the Company.  \n \n \n********** \n Roorkee had visited the State on 5 th June’ 2017 and held discussions with State Government\nofficials. An aerial survey of the reach of river Ganga from Buxar to Farakka was carried out by\nthe Central team.\nThe team held discussions with Hon’ble Chief Minister of Bihar along with State\nGovernment officials and experts wherein it was decided that a Committee to look into various\naspects of floods and siltation in the State of Bihar shall be constituted. The opinion of State\nGovernment of Bihar has also been obtained in respect of constitution of the Committee\nincluding its Terms of Reference.\nConsequently, a Committee has been constituted under the Chairmanship of Shri A.B.\nPandya, Former Chairman, Central Water Commission (CWC), to address the issues of flood and\nsiltation in the State of Bihar. The Committee was constituted on 24th August, 2017.\n(d) Erosion and deposition of silt is a natural process in alluvial rivers. Rivers carry, pickup and\ndrop silt load as per their regime conditions , i.e. discharge in the river, river slope, morphology,\nnature of silt etc. A Committee headed by Dr. B.K. Mittal, former Chairman, CWC had studied\nthe siltation pattern in few rivers in India and inter -alia concluded that siltation was not\npronounced and alarm ing. The Committee also found that de -silting in general was not feasible\ntechnically due to several reasons like non -sustainability,\nnon-availability of vast land required for the disposal of dredged material etc. However, cost\neffective measures for rem oval of drainage congestion in specific reaches of rivers for channel\ncapacity improvement and navigation purposes are formulated and implemented by concerned\nStates/ agencies as per requirement. The Union Government renders assistance to States which is\ntechnical, advisory, catalytic and promotional in nature.\n(e) No, Madam. The Government has not fixed any time limit for removal of the silt deposits.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |544", "t": "Acquisition of Aircraft by Air India", "head": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 544 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nLIVESTOCK  BREEDING \n \n544. SHRI  LAKHAN LAL SAHU: \n \n        Will the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE क ृ षि एवं ककसान कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether livestock breeding for milk production is no longer a profitable occupation specially for \nsmall and marginal farmers of the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the steps taken by the Government to make the cattle rearing a profitable occupation? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \n(SHRIMATI  KRISHNA  RAJ) \n \n(a)&(b):  No, Sir.  Milk production in the country has grown at the rate of 5.78% annually \nbetween 2014-15 and 2016-17 (increased from 143.6 million tonnes during 2014-15 to 163.7 million \ntonnes during 2016 -17) and its benefit goes to 70 million rural household enga ged in dairying \nincluding 52.67 million small and marginal farmers. The gross value added from the milk group at \nthe current basic has increased from Rs.3.28 lakh crores to Rs.4.92 lakh crores between 2011-12 and \n2014-15. This shows that milk production is  viable and profitable occupation both for small and \nmarginal farmers and others.  \n \n(c): In order to supplement and complement the efforts made by the States in making milk \nproduction profitable and also to provide benefits to farmers for cattle & buffalo breeding; livestock \nhealth; animal nutrition and livestock insurance Government is implementing following programmes \n/ schemes: \ni. Rashtriya Gokul Mission (National Programme for Bovine Breeding, Indigenous Breeds \nand National Mission on Bovine Productivity) \nii. Dairy Entrepreneurship Development Scheme \niii. National Programme for Dairy Development \niv. National Dairy Plan-I \nv. National Livestock Mission \nvi. Livestock Health & Disease Control Programme  \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |545", "t": "Capacity Addition by NTPC", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS \n \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-545 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2018 \n \n \nFUNCTIONING OF PARLIAMENT \n \n \n545. SHRI K. PARASURAMAN: \n \nWill the Minister of Parliamentary Affairs be pleased to state:-  \n \n(a) Whether the Government has taken/proposes to take fresh initiatives to discuss in the Parliament \nregarding the holistic assessment of efficiency based on different parameters like the numbe r of \nsittings, Bills passed, Bill held up, the extent of participation of members, duration of debates on each \nBill etc.; and  \n(b) If so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS; AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER \nDEVELOPMENT AND GANGA REJUVENATION. \n \n(Shri Arjun Ram Meghwal) \n \n(a) No Madam.   \n \n(b) Does not arise \n \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |546", "t": "Maintenance/Upgradation of NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 546 \nANSWERED ON 05THAPRIL, 2018 \n \nMAINTENANCE/UPGRADATION OF NHs \n                                                          \n* 546.  SHRIMATI PRATYUSHA RAJESHWARI SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the agencies responsible for repair and maintenance/upgradation of National \nHighways (NHs) in Odisha  and the time by which the work in this regard is likely to \nbe started;  \n(b) whether the Government has entrusted the maintenance and upgradation of road to \nfour lane standard to National Highway Authority of India (NHAI) under different \nprogrammes in Odisha; and  \n(c) if so, the details of stretches entrusted to NHAI for improvement under different \nprogrammes? \n \nANSWER \n \n    THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY  OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 546 FOR ANSWER ON 05 THAPRIL, 2018 ASKED BY \nSHRIMATI PRATYUSHA RAJESHWARI SINGH  REGARDING \nMAINTENANCE/UPGRADATION OF NHs. \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n(a) National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) and National Highways wing of \nState PWD are responsible for repair and maintenance/upgradation of N ational \nHighways (NHs) in Odisha. The development and maintenance of NHs is a \ncontinuous process. The works on NHs, including those in the State of Odisha, are, \naccordingly, taken up from time to time as per inter -se priority, traffic density and \navailability of funds. \n(b)  Yes, Madam. \n(c)    1912 km length of National Highways in the State of Odisha has been entrusted to \nNHAI for maintenance and up gradation under different programmes. The details \nof stretches entrusted to NHAI are at Annexure-I  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (b) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 546 FOR ANSWER ON 05 THAPRIL, 2018 ASKED BY \nSHRIMATI PRATYUSHA RAJESHWARI SINGH  REGARDING \nMAINTENANCE/UPGRADATION OF NHs. \n \nDetails OF NHs entrusted to NHAI in the State of Odisha \n \nNH \nNo.(New) \nNH \nNo.(Old) Description Length \n(km) \n16  60  Wb/Orissa Border To Balasore  53.41 \n16  5  Balasore– Orissa/Ap Border  391.53 \n53  5A  Chandikhole – Paradip  77.00  \n20/520  215  Panikoili – Rimuli – Roxy – Rajamunda  262.62  \n53 /149 200/23  Chandikhole – Duburi – Talcher  133.00  \n316  203  Bhubaneswar – Puri  67.26 \n55  42  Cuttack – Angul – Sambalpur  265.00  \n53  6  Sambalpur – Bargarh  88.00  \n143  23  Biramitrapur – Barkote  125.62 \n49/53  6  Baharagora – Sambalpur  368.00 \n18  5  Baleshwar-Baripada-Jharpokharia  80.60 \nTotal 1912.04 \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |547", "t": "Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 547 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 05.04.2018 \nPRADHAN MANTRI GRAM SADAK YOJANA \n \n*547.  KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV: \n \n Will the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has reviewed the progre ss made in the implementation of the \nPradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY), if so, th e details and the outcome \nthereof including the targets fixed and the achieve ments under the scheme during the \nlast three years;  \n(b)  whether the Government has fixed any time fram e to speed up the execution of rural \nroads so as to achieve full rural connectivity by M arch, 2019 and if so, the details \nthereof along with the number of habitations covere d by all weather roads under \nPMGSY so far and the number of habitations yet to b e covered along with the steps \ntaken by the Government to cover those habitations;  \n(c)  whether some of the States are facing problems  in implementing the scheme, if so, the \ndetails thereof and the reasons therefor along with  the steps proposed to be taken by \nthe Government to help those States to overcome the problems, State-wise;  \n(d)  whether deficiencies in the construction of ro ads under the scheme have come to the \nnotice of the Government during the last three year s, if so, the details thereof and the \nsteps taken by the Government to remove those deficiencies; and  \n(e)  whether the Government has launched Geographic  Information System (GIS) based \nmapping of all rural roads, if so, the details ther eof and the time by which the said \nmapping is likely to be completed? \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) to (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of th e House.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.547  \nfor answer on 05.4.2018 \n \n(a): The status of progress made in implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY) is  regularly reviewed in the  Regional Rev iew Meetings (RRMs), Performance Review \nMeeting (PRC), Pre-Empowered Committee and Empowere d Committee Meetings with the States. \nAlso, at District level, the District Development C oordination and Monitoring Committee (Disha) \nheaded by a Member of Parliament monitors the imple mentation of various schemes of \nGovernment of India including PMGSY.  In addition t o this, special review meetings are also held \nby Secretary/Additional Secretary, Ministry of Rura l Development with Chief Secretaries of the \nStates.  Review meetings were also held by the Mini ster of Rural Development on 15 th  December, \n2017 and 28 th  February, 2018.  \nThe target fixed and achievements under the scheme during the last three years are as follows:- \nYear Length (in Km) \nTarget Achievement \n2014-15 21,775 36,337 \n2015-16 33,649 36,449 \n2016-17 48,812 47,447 \n \n(b):  The Government of India has taken a decision to accelerate execution of PMGSY-I to provide \nconnectivity to eligible habitations as per the Cor e Network of PMGSY by March, 2019.  The \nnumber of eligible unconnected habitations as per t he Core Network is 1,78,184, out of which \n1,63,429 habitations have been sanctioned by the Mi nistry (till February,2018).  The States have \nreported that 1,30,415 habitations  have been conne cted  till February, 2018. The State \nGovernments have been requested to get approval for  sanction of balance works of New \nConnectivity and upgradation under PMGSY-I as per m andate of the scheme and complete them \nlatest by March, 2019 so as to provide connectivity to all eligible unconnected habitations. \n \n(c): The problems being faced by some of  States as  reported by them , inter-alia, include:  \n \n(i) Difficult terrain particularly in Hill States and N orth-Eastern States; shorter working \nseason; \n(ii) Scarcity of the construction materials \n \n \n \n\nThe Ministry of Rural Development has taken a numbe r of initiatives to meet the above challenges \nfaced by the States. The Ministry has engaged Centr al Public Sector Undertakings (CPSUs) in \nsome of the States to augment execution capacity of  the States. The Ministry has also conducted \nnumber of Contractor’s Outreach Programmes in the S tates to attract the Contractors in the \nimplementation of the Programme. Further, in order to encourage locally available materials and \nuse of green technologies,  guidelines were issued by the Ministry, wherein the State  Governments \nare required to propose minimum 15% of total length  of annual proposals under New technologies \nsuch as Cement stabilization, Lime stabilization, C old mix, Waste plastics, Cell filled concrete, \nPaneled cement concrete pavement, Fly ash etc. The Ministry is also in constant touch with the \nState Governments and other stake holders to addres s the security concerns for smooth \nimplementation of PMGSY. \n              \n(d): No specific deficiency in the construction of roads "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |548", "t": "Use of Diesel Gensets for Power Generation", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS & FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 548 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06th February, 2018 \n \nViolation of Stent Prices \n \n548. DR. P.K. BIJU: \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that private hospitals are overcharging their \npatients for angioplasty despite the fact that the Government has slashed the \nprices of cardiac stents to the tune of 75 per cent; \n \n(b) if so, the number of complaints received by the National Pharmaceutical Pricing \nAuthority in this regard against such hospitals; and \n \n(c) the action taken by the Government against the management of the said private \nhospitals? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS; \nMINISTRY OF SHIPPING AND MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) to (c): National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority (NPPA) vide its notification S.O. \n412(E), dated 13 th February, 2017 fixed the ceiling price of the coronary stents. \nInstitutions such as hospitals/nursing homes/clinics utilizing Coronary Stents for \nangioplasty are bound to abide by the ceiling prices fixed by the Government for \ncoronary stents and NPPA has not found any actionable violation after examining about \n40 complaints. The Government is effectively monitoring the implementation of ceiling \nprices fixed for coronary stents.   \n \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |549", "t": "Gap between MGNREGS and State Wages", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 549 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 05.04.2018 \nGAP BETWEEN MGNREGS AND STATE WAGES \n \n*549.  SHRI Y.S. AVINASH REDDY: \n \n Will the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to reduce the gap between the wages under the \nMahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) and \nthe state wages;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof, Statewise; and  \n(c)  whether the Government has taken the opinion o f the States in this regard and if so, \nthe details thereof? \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n(a) to (c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of th e House.  \n \n \n***** \n \n \n  \n\n \nStatement in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha  Starred Question No. 549 for \n05.04.2018 \n \n(a) to (c):        No such decision has been taken.  As per section 6(1) of Mahatma \nGandhi National Rural Emp \nloyment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), 2005, the Central Government notifies \nMGNREGA wage rates every year for all States/UTs. The wage rates are revised and \napplicable from 1st  April every year. The revision is based on Consume r Price Index \nfor Agricultural Labour (CPI-AL).   \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |55", "t": "Public Distribution System Network", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 55    \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM NETWORK \n \n*55.  SHRI PRATHAP SIMHA:  \nKUMARI SHOBHA KARANDLAJE:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether a new central sector scheme has recently been approved for \nestablishing Public Distribution System Network (PDSN) to implement \nnational level portability, central data repository and central monitoring \nsystem of PDS operations and the same is proposed to be implemented \nduring the financial years 2018-19 and 2019-20 and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b)  whether a pilot scheme on Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) on the \npattern of “PAHAL” has also been launched recently and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n \n(c)  whether the subsidy amount under this scheme is directly transferred \ninto the bank account of the eligible beneficiaries under the National Food \nSecurity Act, 2013 in advance in the beginning of the month; \n \n(d)  the time by which the scheme is likely to be implemented in all the \nStates; and  \n \n(e)  the names of the States where the facility enabling PDS beneficiaries \nto lift their entitled foodgrains from any Fair Price Shop in the State has been \nstarted? \n \n \n \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI RAMVILAS PASWAN) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n***  \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e ) OF \nTHE STARRED QUESTION NO. 55* DUE FOR ANSWER ON \n06.02.2018 IN THE LOK SABHA.  \n(a): A new central sector scheme by the name ‘Integrated \nManagement of Public Distribution System’ (IM -PDS) has been \napproved for implementation during 2018- 19 and 2019- 20 at total \ncost of Rs. 127.30 crore. The key objectives of scheme are: \n• Implementation of nation- wide portability in food grains \ndistribution. \n• Implementation of national level data repository for de-\nduplication of beneficiary data (Aadhaar numbers).  \n• Integration of National PDS portal with State Transparency \nportals and creation of integrated data infrastructure \nsystems developed for ration card management, allocation, \nsupply chain, FPS automation, etc.  \n• Employing advanced data analytics techniques on \ncentralized databases to bring about continuous \nimprovements in PDS operations. \n• Developing advanced web and mobile based applications to \nimprove user-friendly PDS operations. \n• Improving the quality of implementation by introducing new \nquality standards and benchmarks and providing handholding \nsupport to States/UTs. \n• Facilitating cross -learning and sharing of best practices \namong States/UTs. \n(b) to (d):  A pilot scheme on Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) on the \npattern of “PAHAL” has been launched in Nagri Block of Ranchi \nDistrict w.e.f. 01.10.2017 under which subsidy component is \ncredited into the benef iciaries’ bank account and beneficiaries \npurchase foodgrains from FPSs. This scheme has been launched on \npilot basis in Nagri block of Ranchi district in Jharkhand State. No \ndecision has been taken regarding the roll out of the scheme in \nother States. \n(e):  States of Andhra Pradesh, Delhi, Haryana, Karnataka (partial), \nMaharashtra (partial) and Telangana (partial) have enabled facility \nfor intra-state portability.  \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |550", "t": "DTH Service Providers", "head": "\u0003\n\u0003\n\u0003\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK  SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO.  550 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 06, 2018 \n \nFUNDS FOR RAJASTHAN \n \nNo. 550. SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to release the second \ninstalment of Rs. 6.67 crore to Rajasthan for implementation \nof the third phase under the Integrated Housing and Slum \nDevelopment programme; \n(b)  if so, the time by which the funds are likely to be released; \nand   \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY \nOF HOUSING & URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (c) Under the Integrated Housing and Slum Development \nProgramme (IHSDP) of Jawaharlal Nehru National Urban Renewal \nMission (JNNURM), release of Rs. 6. 67 crores as second and final \ninstallment of Additional Central Assistance (ACA) for one phase \nthree project at Kota, Rajasthan  could not be made within the \nmission period for want of certain cl arifications including Financial \nClosure Certificate giving details of tender cost of housing and \ninfrastructure, from the concerned Department of the State \nGovernment. The extended period of JNNURM ended on 31 March \n2017 and as such, there is no provision for releasing ACA in \nJNNURM projects further. \n**** \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |551", "t": "Power Supply to Domestic Consumers", "head": "������������������� �\n�������������������������������������� �\n���������� �\n������������������������� �\n������ �� ������ �� ��������������� �\n�\n�������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������ �\n��\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ ��� ����������� �������� ��� ����� ����������� �������� �������� ����� ��� �������\n���������������� ������������������ ���������� �������� ������ ������������ �������� ���������� ������ ������������ ������������������ ������ ���������������� ����������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� �����������������������������\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ��� ���������� ���� ��������������� ��� ���� ����� �����������\n�������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ��� ������������� ������� ������� ��� ������� ���� ����� �����������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ���������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n������ �\n�\n���������������������������������������������������� �\n����������������� �������\n�\n����������� ����������� ��� ���������� �������� �������� ������ ���� ��������������������\n������� ������ ��������������������������������� ����������� ��� ���������� ����������� ����\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���������� ��� ��������� ��� ������ �������� ������� �������� �������� �������� ������ ������\n������������������� �\n�\n������������ ������ ���� �������� ��� ������������� ��� ����� ����������� ����������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������� ��������������� ��������������� ������ ������ ��������������� ����� ��������� ���������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������� ������ ��� ���� ����������� ����� ������� � ��������� ���� ��������� ���� �����������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������\n�\n����"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |552", "t": "Installation of Rooftop Solar Grid", "head": "������������������� �\n������������������������������������ �\n��������� �\n������������������� �����\n����������������� ������������\n�\n���������� ������������������������ �\n�\n���������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������������������� ���� �����������������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������\n������ �\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������� �\n������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |553", "t": "Production of Solar Energy", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 553 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 06, 2018 \n \nGAMBHIR COMMITTEE \n \nNo. 553 KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV: \n  \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state:- \n \n(a) whether  Justice Gambhir Committee report has been submitted to the \nGovernment; \n(b) if so, the findings of the report on the issue of non-utilization or diversion \nof funds allocated for the scheme for providing shelters to the urban \nhomeless;  \n(c) the number of existing shelters that comply with the operational \nguidelines of National Urban Livelihood Mission (NULM);  \n(d) whether the Committee’s recommendations have been implemented; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF  \nTHE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN AFFAIRS \n[SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI] \n***** \n(a) & (b): Justice (Retired) Kailash Gambhir Committee report was submitted \nto the Hon’ble Supreme Court on 10 July, 2017. It points out that though there \nare funds that have not been spent but yet it cannot be termed as mis-utilized \nor diversion of funds. \n \n(c): The DAY-NULM is being implemented by States/ UTs. While sanctioning \nshelters, the State Project Sanction Committee is to ensure projects are as \nper DAY-NULM guidelines.  As per gui delines, States/ ULBs would undertake \nperiodical quality audit of operational shel ters. As intimated by States/UTs, a \ntotal of 1331 shelters have been sanctioned by 25 States/UTs under DAY-\nNULM out of which 789 shelters are operational.   \n \n(d)& (e): The Committee report was circulated to all States/UTs. Further, in \naccordance with the recommendations of the Committee, actions taken \ninclude creation of a central portal for uploading profiles of shelters, issue of \ndirections to States/ UTs for conducting a third party survey of urban \nhomeless and also to keep funds earmarked/ allocated for Shelter for Urban \nHomeless component, out of DAY-NULM funds, in a separate account.   \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |554", "t": "Sale of Land Assets by AAI", "head": " \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 534 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nINVESTMENT IN CONTRACT FARMING \n \n534.  DR. P. VENUGOPAL:  \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE   कृषि एवं ककसान कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is considering to encourage private sector investment in \ncontract farming and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b)  whether the Government has received any proposals in this regard  and if so, the details \nthereof; and  \n \n(c)  whether the contract farming is helpful in utilisation of the land remained unutilised for a \nlong time and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nकृषि एवं ककसान कल्याण मंत्राऱय में राज्य मंत्री     (SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT) \n \n(a): Twenty States have made provisions for Contract Farming in their State Agricultural \nProduce Marketing Committee (APMC) Acts following the provision in model APMC Act,  2003 \ncirculated by the Government of India for adoption.  Under model APMC Act, 2003, Market \nCommittee or a prescribed officer has been designated as registering, agreement recording and \ndispute settlement authority. Apart from 20 States, Punjab has formu lated a separate Contract \nFarming Act. Contract Farming is being implemented by States as per the provisions of the \nrespective State’s APMC Act. Contract Farming is already operational in States such as \nMaharashtra, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh and Haryana.   \n \n(b): In view of above, no proposal has been received by the Government of India. \n \n(c): Yes. Under the contract farming, Horticulture, Apiculture, Sericulture and animal \nhusbandry etc. defined as agricultural produce under the APMC Act are covered under c ontract \nfarming activities.  The land remained unutilised for a long time can be utilised under contract \nfarming through cultivating the crop/ rearing the live stock on such land unsuitable for growing \nstaple crops. \n \n*********** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |555", "t": "Production of Solar Energy", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 555 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nSETTING UP OF INTEGRATED CHECK POSTS \n \n555. SHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is considering to set up 13 new Integrated Check \nPosts to encourage India’s engagements with its neighbours belonging to \nSAARC region;  \n \n(b) if so, the details and objectives thereof; \n \n(c) whether it is true that while facilitating legitimate trade and commerce, \nthe borders at the same time needs to be secured against interests hostile to \nthe country; and \n \n(d) if so, the measures taken thereon? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n(a) & (b): Yes Madam . The Government has already set up and \noperationalised five Integrated Check Posts (ICPs) at Attari (Punjab), Agartala \n(Tripura), Petrapole (West Bengal), Raxaul (Bihar) and Jog bani (Bihar). \nGovernment has also approved setting up of ICPs at Moreh (Manipur) and \nDawki (Meghalaya) . T he objective s behind setting up of ICPs are  to provide \nsecure, seamless and efficient system for cargo and passenger movement.  \nDecision to put up more  ICPs is taken based on volume of trade, number of \npassengers, potential for future growth of passengers and cargo traffic, etc. \nSuch decisions are taken by Government after extensive inter -ministerial \nconsultations and analysis with the aim to improve bil ateral trade, relations \nand enhance security. \n\n \n-2- \nLS.US.Q.No.555 FOR 06.02.2018 \n(c) & (d): The Government has established the Land Ports Authority of India \nunder the LPAI Act, 2010 with the objective to put in place systems which \naddress security imperatives and for the development and management of \nfacilities for cross border movement of passengers and goods at designated \npoints along the International borders of the Country. \nThe ICPs are set up as a sanitized zone with dedicated passenger and car go \nterminals comprising adequate customs and immigration facilities, security \nand scanning equipments, health and quarantine facilities along with \npassenger amenities. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |556", "t": "Handling/Operating Capacity of Airports", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 556 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 6th February, 2018 \n \nSub-standard Drugs \n \n556. SHRI Y.V. SUBBA REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is true that as per the recent National Drug Survey 2014 -16, more than \n3% of drugs sold in the country are below quality standards;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the percentage of such drugs sold is nearly 11% in Andhra Pradesh and the \npractice is more prominent in Government hospitals; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the manner in which the Government is planning to \ndirect Andhra Pradesh and other States where drug quality is below standards? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS; \nMINISTRY OF SHIPPING AND MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n(SHRI MANSUKH L. MANDAVIYA) \n \n(a) & (b): As per the National Drug Survey Report 2014 -16, total 3.16% of the drug \nsamples were found to be Not of Standard Quality (NSQ). \n(c) & (d): As per the survey report, 10.64% of drug samples were found to be NSQ in \nthe State of Andhra Pradesh from Government sources. In the said survey, ove rall \n10.02% (total 839 out of the 8369 samples) of the drug samples drawn from \nGovernment sources were found Not of Standard Quality (NSQ). The test Reports of \nthe drug samples declared as Not of Standard Quality (NSQ) were forwarded to \nconcerned State Licensing Authorities with a request to take appropriate action and also \nto take legal samples of same batch of drugs for testing. \nxxxxx \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|STARRED   |557", "t": "Construction/Upgradation of Airports", "head": "                      \n \n                                                      \n          \n                  \n \n                                                                                 \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPA\nRTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n557\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n6\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, 20\n1\n8\n \n \nSALE OF PULSES\n \n \n557. \n \n \nSHRI ARKA KESHARI DEO:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the production of different\n \nvarieties of puls\nes is likely to increase during \nthe \ncurrent year in the country;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof, State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the farmers are \nsellin\ng these pulses especially Tur dal in\n \nth\ne open market below \nthe Minimum \nSupport Price (MSP) set by the\n \nGovernment; and\n \n \n(d\n)\n \n \nif so, the steps taken by the \nGovernment to protect these farmers?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FAR\nMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nGAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT\n)\n \n \n(a) & (b):\n \n \nIt is early to have a firm assessment of increase or decrease of total production of \npulses in 2017\n-\n18 for the current year as the Second Advance estimate cov\nering both Kharif and \nRabi pulses are normally released in mid\n-\nFebruary.\n \n \nA\ns per first advance estimate 2017\n-\n18, the production of Kharif\n \npulses is estimated at 8.71 \nmillion tonnes which is lower by 0.72 million tonnes than the last year’s record productio\nn of 9.42 \nmillion tonnes (as per fourth advance estimate 2016\n-\n17). However, kharif pulses estimated \nproduction in 2017\n-\n18 is 2.86 million tonnes more than average production of five years ending \n2015\n-\n16. The State\n-\nwise details of production of different ma\njor varieties of kharif pulses for the \ncurrent year and previous year are given at \nAnnexure\n.\n \n \n(c)\n:\n \n \nDuring the agricultural year 2017\n-\n18 (July\n-\nJune) the all\n-\nIndia average wholesale prices \n(July 2017 to January 2018) of pulses such as urad, masur and gram w\nas above the minimum \nsupport price (MSP). However, the average wholesale prices of Tur and Moong, was below the \nMSP during the same period.\n  \n \n \n(d):\n \n \nGovernment implements Price Stabilization Fund (PSF) and Price Support Schemes \n(PSS) to protect the interes\nt of farmers. Under the PSF, procurement of pulses for central buffer \nis undertaken at market prices or MSP, whichever is higher\n. \nFurther, PSS is \nimplemented\n \nfor \nprocurement through Central Nodal Agencies at the MSP wherein State Agencies play a major \nrole\n. The PSS is implemented \nat the request of the State Government\ns concerned.\n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 557 due \nfor reply on 06.02.2018\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nState\n-\nwise Production of Kharif Pulses\n \n \n('000 Tonnes)\n \nState\n \nTur\n \nUrad\n \nMoong\n \nTotal Pulses\n \n2017\n-\n18$\n \n2016\n-\n17*\n \n2017\n-\n18$\n \n2016\n-\n17*\n \n2017\n-\n18$\n \n2016\n-\n17*\n \n2017\n-\n18$\n \n2016\n-\n17*\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n113.0\n \n132.0\n \n34.0\n \n49.0\n \n15.0\n \n17.0\n \n207.0\n \n205.0\n \nAssam\n \n5.0\n \n6.0\n \n35.0\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n40.0\n \n6.0\n \nBihar\n \n34.2\n \n37.1\n \n13.4\n \n13.7\n \n8.4\n \n7.6\