 \nMahal and whether this cap is also applicable on foreign tourists and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and\n \n(f)\n \nthe other steps taken/being taken by the Government to protect the\n \nworld heritage \nmonument of Taj Mahal?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR CULTURE AND \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n(a)to(c)\n      \nNo, Madam.\n \n \ncontd…….2/\n-\n \n \n\n \n \n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n \n(d)\n \nA preliminary notification for new ticket price at Taj Mahal has\n \nbeen notified on \n21.12.2017.  As per the notification the rates are as follows:\n \n \n \nCashless\n \n \nCash\n \nCitizen of India and visitors from \nSAARC and BIMSTEC countries\n \n \nRs.35/\n-\n \nper head\n \nRs.40/\n-\n \nper head\n \nOther nationals\n \n \nRs.550/\n-\n \nper head\n \nRs.600/\n-\n \nper head\n \nOthe\nr nationals (for additional \nfacilities)\n \nRs.800/\n-\n \nper head\n \nRs.850/\n-\n \nper head\n \n \n \n(e)\n \nNo, Madam.\n \n \n(f)\n \nThe conservation and preservation works are being taken up as per approved \nprogram and availability of funds.  The security management is being done by \nCen\ntral Industrial Security Force.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |375", "t": "Untrained Teachers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.375 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 21ST MARCH, 2018 \n \nIMPORT  OF  WEAPONS \n \n*375. SHRI  VENKATESH  BABU  T.G.:     \n     \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE   j{kk ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether India has become t he world ’s largest importer of weapons and military \nequipment; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  the details of weapons and military equipment imported during the last three years \nalong with the value / cost thereof? \n \n \nA    N    S    W    E    R \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                    (SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN)  \n      j{kk ea=h                  ¼Jherh  fueZyk lhrkje.k) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n******* \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a)  TO (c) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 375 FOR ANSWER ON 21.3.2018 \n \n(a) to (c): No authoritative and official information on India being the \nlargest importer of defence equipment is available as no country officially \nreveals information on the import of  defence equipment.  However, in the \nreport published in February 2017 by the Stockholm International Peace \nResearch Institute (SIPRI), India has been shown as the largest importer of \ndefence equipment for the years 2012-16. \nCapital procurement of defence equipment is undertaken from \nvarious domestic as well as foreign vendors, based on threat perception, \noperational challenges and technological changes and to keep the Armed \nForces in        a state of readiness to meet the entire spectrum of security \nchallenges. \nDuring the last three years, 96 contracts have been signed with \nIndian vendors and 58 contracts have been signed with foreign vendors for \ncapital procurement of defence equipment for Armed Forces.  The major \nDefence equipment imported include missil es, aircraft, artillery guns, \nradars, rockets, helicopters, weapons and simulators. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |376", "t": "Setting up of LNG Terminal", "head": " \nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d ) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 376 FOR ANSWER ON 21.3.2018 \n \n(a) & (b):  Casualty data maintained is as per the notified operational \nareas.  Details regar ding death of soldiers in Siachen Glacier during last \none decade are as under:- \nYear \n \nCasualty \nOfficers JCOs / ORs \n2008 - 09 \n2009 - 13 \n2010 - 50 \n2011 02 22 \n2012 01 11 \n2013 - 11 \n2014 01 07 \n2015 01 10 \n2016 01 19 \n2017 - 05 \n2018 - - \n \nCauses of de ath in Siachen Glacier and other Super High \nAltitude Areas range from those directly related to high \naltitude like High Altitude Pulmonary Oedema (HAPO), High \nAltitude cerebral Oedema (HACO) and Pulmonary Thrombo \nEmbolism (PTE) to other general causes. \n(c) & (d):  Indian Army soldiers deployed in extremely harsh terrain and \nweather conditions are suitably equipped and properly trained to \nundertake  operational challenges and carry out their mandated tasks.  The \nsoldiers deployed at Siachen Glacier are provi ded with best quality winter \nclothing including ‘Extreme Cold Climate ’ clothing. Besides, they are \nprovided with prefabricated insulated shelters and wherever it is not \npossible to construct such shelters due to technical difficulties, insulated \ntents are provided  which can withstand low temperatures upto -50o  \nCelsius. \n \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |377", "t": "Relaxation of FDI Norms", "head": "��������������\n�������������������\n����������������������������\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.377\n�����������������������������\nH1B AND L1 VISAS\n���������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������\n��� ������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������\n��� �����������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ������������������������������������������������������������� ����\n������������ � ������ � ������� � ���� � �� � �� � �������������� � ������� � ���\n������������������������������������������������\n���