HANDRA ALIAS HARISH DWIVEDI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether incidents of jail breaks  have been reported from various parts of  \nthe country; \n \n(b) if so, the number of such cases reported during each of the last three years, \nand the current year, State-wise; \n \n(c) whether the Government has issued  guidelines about prison security with  \nparticular instructions for placing of terrorists in high security jails; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (b):  State/UT wise details of the incidents of Jail breaks during the years \n2014 to 2016, compiled by the National Crimes Record Bureau, are given in the \nStatement at Annex-I.  \n \n(c) & (d):  The Government of India has been providing guidance to States and \nUTs on prison security in the form of guidelines and advisories issued from \ntime to time.  The advisories include guidance on improving security measures \nin jails to avoid the in cidents of jail break. The advisories are available on the \nwebsite of the Ministry of Home Affairs at: \nhttp://mha1.nic.in/PrisonReforms/home.html.   \n \n \n \n\n \n-2- \nLS.US.Q.No.583 FOR 06.02.2018 \n \nThe Ministry of Home Affairs had also prepared and circulated a Model Prison \nManual in 2016 which has dedicated chapters/ guidance on Custodial \nManagement and High Risk Offenders and Detenues.  The Manual was sent to \nall States with the objective of servin g as a useful tool for prison \nadministration and also to serve as a benchmark that all States can seek \nguidance from. \n  \n\n \nLS.US.Q.No.583 FOR 06.02.2018 \n \nAnnexure-I \n \nState/UT-wise Incidence of Jail breaks during 2014 – 2016 \n \nSl. \nNo. State/UT \nIncidence of Jail Breaks \n2014 2015 2016  \n(Provisional) \n(1) (2) (3) (4) (5) \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 0 0 0 \n2 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 0 0 0 \n3 ASSAM 0 0 0 \n4 BIHAR 0 0 1 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 0 0 1 \n6 GOA 0 0 0 \n7 GUJARAT 0 1 1 \n8 HARYANA 0 1 0 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 2 1 0 \n10 JAMMU & KASHMIR 0 0 0 \n11 JHARKHAND 0 0 0 \n12 KARNATAKA 0 0 0 \n13 KERALA 0 0 0 \n14 MADHYA PRADESH 1 0 4 \n15 MAHARASHTRA 0 0 0 \n16 MANIPUR 0 0 0 \n17 MEGHALAYA 0 1 0 \n18 MIZORAM 1 0 0 \n19 NAGALAND 1 1 0 \n20 ODISHA 0 0 0 \n21 PUNJAB 0 1 1 \n22 RAJASTHAN 0 1 2 \n23 SIKKIM 0 0 0 \n24 TAMIL NADU 0 0 0 \n25 TELANGANA 0 0 0 \n26 TRIPURA 0 0 3 \n27 UTTAR PRADESH 6 7 0 \n28 UTTARAKHAND 0 0 0 \n29 WEST BENGAL 0 0 0 \n TOTAL (STATES) 11 14 13 \n30 A & N ISLANDS 0 0 0 \n31 CHANDIGARH 0 0 0 \n32 D & N HAVELI 5 0 0 \n33 DAMAN & DIU 0 0 0 \n34 DELHI 0 1 0 \n35 LAKSHADWEEP 0 0 0 \n36 PUDUCHERRY 0 0 0 \n TOTAL (UTs) 5 1 0 \n TOTAL (ALL-INDIA) 16 15 13 \nSource: Prison Statistics India "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |584", "t": "Agricultural Crisis", "head": "                                                                                                            \nO.I.H\n                 \n \n                                                                                 \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINIS\nTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n584\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n6\nTH\n \nF\nEBRUARY\n, 20\n1\n8\n \n \nAGRICULTURAL CRISIS\n \n \n584. \n \nSHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL:\n \nSHRIMATI RANJANBEN BHA\nTT:\n \nSHRI SANJAY HARIBHAU JADHAV:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has\n \nconducted \nany study to identify the areas \nwhich are fa\ncing \nagricultural crisis in th\ne \ncountry;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and the outcome\n \nthereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nthe\n \nsteps taken/being taken by the \nGov\nernment to solve the problem of \nagricultural crisis \nin the country; and\n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government \nproposes to promote the use of modern\n \nagr\nicultural\n \ntechniques \ninstead of \nconv\nentional method for sustainable \ngrowth and development in the agriculture\n \nsector and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nGAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT\n)\n \n \n(a) & (b): \n \nNo, Madam.\n \n \n(c):\n \n \nAgrarian distress as manifest from large number of farmers living below the poverty \n(BPL) line and unfortunate incidents of suicides can be \naddressed by enabling the farmers to \nincrease their income.  Agriculture is state subject. However, the Government is targeting to \ndouble the income of the farmers by the year 2022.  To achieve this, the Department of \nAgriculture, Cooperation and Farmers’ \nWelfare has constituted an Inter\n-\nMinisterial Committee to \nexamine various dimensions of farmers’ income and to recommend an appropriate strategy.  In \nthe meanwhile, the Government is realigning its interventions to focus on income of farmers in \naddition to\n \nbetter production issues. The Department is, therefore, implementing various \nschemes to meet this objective viz. Soil Health Card (SHC) scheme, Neem Coated Urea, \nParamparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY), Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana (PMKSY), \nNation\nal Agriculture Market Scheme (e\n-\n \nNAM), Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), \nInterest Subvention Scheme etc.\n \nContd..2/\n-\n \n \n \n\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n(d): \n \nScheme on Submission on Agricultural  Mechanisation (SMAM) is being operated in \nwhich  financial assistance as cost su\nbsidy is being provided for individual ownership of farm \nmachinery. \n \n \n          \nIn order to achieve fast paced growth and increasing agricultural production\n, \nthe Indian \nCouncil of Agricultural Research (ICAR) has prioritized research and development progra\nmmes \nin rice\n, \nwheat, maize\n, \nmillets\n, \nfodder crops\n, \noilseeds\n, \npulses\n, \nsugarcane\n, \ncotton and other fiber \ncrops\n.\n \n \n           \nThe crop\n· \nimprovement programmes lay emphasis on development of new crop \nvarieties\n/\nhybrid\ns \nwith improved quality and tolerance\n/\nresista\nnce to biotic and abiotic stresses \nand enabling crops to withstand extremities of weather. \n \n \n \n           \nImproved varieties and production technologies were also demonstrated at the farmers\n' \nfield\ns \nb\ny \nthe ICAR institut\ne\ns\n, \nState Agricultural Universities (S\nAUs) and Krishi Vig\ny\nan Kendras \n(KVKs) through frontline demonstration\ns \n(FLD) programme to create awareness among \nfarmers. \n \n \n            \nKisan Suvidha Mobile App has been launched by the Government which provides \ninformation to farmers on weather, plant protection, input dealers, agro\n-\nadvisory and marketing. \nBesides, Pusa Krishi Mobile App, Agri\n-\nMarket App and Crop Insurance Mob\nile App have also \nbeen launched for the benefit of farmers.\n \n \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |585", "t": "Income of Farmers", "head": "                 \n                  \n \n                                                                                 \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNS\nTARRED QUESTION NO.\n585\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n6\nTH\n \nF\nEBRUARY\n, 20\n1\n8\n \n \nINCOME OF FARMERS\n \n \n585.\n \n \nSHRI SUNIL JAKHAR:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the Chief Economic \nAdvisor, Arvind Subramaniam has reported\n \nthat “R\neal \nincome of farmers producing \ncrops other than cereals are falling’’\n \nand if \nso, the details thereof;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nthe percentage o\nf farmers \nproducing crops other than cereals;\n \n \n(c)\n \n \nwhether the programme for \ndoubling farmers income have failed; and\n \n \n(d)\n \n \nwhe\nther there is any policy course \ncorrections in\n \nthe original plan for doubling \nfarmer\ns \nincome and if so, the details \nthereof?\n \n \nAN\nSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nGAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT\n)\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \n  \nThe views of the Chief Economic Advisor on economic issues are articulated in the \nannual Economic Survey.  The Economic Survey 2017\n-\n18, makes no specific mention r\negarding \n‘fall in real income of farmers producing crops other than cereals’. \n \n \n(b)\n:\n   \nThe details of number of farmers producing crops other than the cereals are not \nmaintained. However, as per the Land Use Statistics 2014\n-\n15, about 49 per cent of the tot\nal \ncropped area in the country is under crops other than cereals and millets. \n \n \n(c) &\n \n(d)\n:\n \n \nNo, Madam. In order to achieve the target of doubling the income of farmers by \n2022, Government has\n \nconstituted an Inter\n-\nMinisterial Committee on 13.04.2016 to examine \nissues relating to doubling of farmers’ income and recommend a strategy to achieve the same \nby the year 2022. Alongside working on a comprehensive strategy, the Committee has been \nsuggest\ning various interventions for consideration. With a view to have an effective \nstakeholders’ participations in finalizing the strategy, the Committee has so far uploaded nine \nVolumes of the draft Report on the website of Department of Agriculture, Cooperati\non and \nFarmers Welfare (http://agricoop.nic.in/doubling\n-\nfarmers) for seeking public opinion.\n \n \n \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |586", "t": "Homeless Persons", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 586 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nHOMELESS PERSONS \n \n586. SHRI CHANDRAKANT KHAIRE: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether 44 homeless persons died  in Delhi in the first week of January this  \nyear; \n \n(b) if so, whether these deaths took  place in the vicinity of the railway stations  \nand hospitals and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the details of the contribution of the Government in constructing night shelters \nfor the homeless? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n (a) & (b) As intimated by Delhi Police, 33 unidentified/homeless pers ons were \nfound dead in Delhi during the first week of January, 2018.  Out of these 33 \npersons, 04 were found dead in the vicinity of hospitals, 03 in the vicinity of \nrailway stations and 26 at other places.  In all the above noted incidents of \ndeaths, inquest proceedings u/s 174 CrPC have been conducted by the local police \nto ascertain the cause of the death. \n(c) As intimated by Government of NCT of Delhi, Delhi Urban Shelter Improvement \nBoard(DUSIB), two night shelters are under construction with the funds  received \nin National Urban Livelihood Mission S cheme. DUSIB has received an amount of \nRs. 2.00 cr under Nat ional Urban Livelihood Mission S cheme for construction of \nnew night shelters. Presently there are 83 Pucca, 115 porta cabin and 66 \ntemporary shelter in tents (for winter season  only) being run by DUSIB with the \nfinancial assistance of GNCTD having total capacity of 21,134 persons.     \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|14|UNSTARRED |587", "t": "Organic Farming", "head": "                  \nO.I.H\n \n                                                                                 \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUEST\nION NO.\n587\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n6\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, 20\n1\n8\n \n \nORGANIC FARMING\n \n \n587.\n \n \nSHRI NIHAL CHAND:\n \nSHRI DILIP PATEL:\n \nSHRI VIRENDER \nKASHYAP:\n \nSHRI JUGAL KISHORE:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe quantum of organic production\n \nand the\n \narea of land thereunder in the \ncountry;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nwhether the Government\n \npropose\ns to promote organic farming on \nthe lines \nof Sikkim \nin other parts of the \ncountry \nas well includin\ng Rajasthan, if so, \nthe details thereof;\n \n \n(c)\n \n \nwhether the Government proposes \nto take \nany steps regarding production, \nmarketing \no\nr organic agricultural products \nand to prov\nide grants for the said purpose \nand if so, the \ndetails thereof;\n \n \n(d\n) \n \nthe action taken \nby the \nGovernment s\no far to bridge the gap between \nthe p\nroducts of \nchemical farming and \norganic farming;\n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether the Government has any\n \nplan or pr\noposal to reduce the production \ncost of \norga\nnic farming so as to popularize \nthe same\n \namong farmers of the \ncountry; \nand\n \n \n(f)\n \n \nthe details of funds allocated and\n \nreleased to \nfarmers for encouraging organic \nfarming \na\nnd the benefits accrued to them \nduring the l\nast three years and the current \nyear, State\n-\nwise?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nGAJENDRA SINGH SEHKHAWAT\n)\n \n \n(a):\n \nThe quantum of organic produce is 1180105.81 MT   during the year 2016\n-\n17 under \nthe National Programme on Organic Production (NPOP\n)\n.\n  \nThe area of organic cultivation\n \nis \n22.5 lakh hactare in the country. The details of organic production & area under cultivation are \ngiven at \nAnnexure\n-\n \nI, I A, I B & I C.\n \nContd..2/\n-\n \n\n \n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n(b) to (e)\n:\n \n \nParampragat Krishi Vikas Yojna a scheme has been  launched since 2015\n-\n16 \nto promote   \norganic farming in clusters mode and make available chemical free inputs to the \nfarmers. Government of India is providing assistance to farmers in all the states including \nRajasthan for organic cultivation, certification, labeling, packing, transportation \nand marketing \nof organic produce under the scheme of Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY). In \naddition, organic value chain development for organic products from production to marketing \nis promoted in North Eastern Region through Mission Organic Value C\nhain Development \n(MOVCD). \n \n \nIn addition, use of organic inputs like PROM, vermicompost, organic/bio\n-\nfertilizers, city \ncompost, waste decomposer have been promoted under various schemes of Government of \nIndia. Use of organic inputs will reduce the cost of p\nroduction when compared to in organic \nfarming.\n \n \n(f):\n \nThe state \n–\n \nwise details of the funds allocated and released under the Schemes PKVY \nand MOVCDNER is given at\n \nAnnexure \n-\n \nII, IIA, III and Ill A.\n \n\nAnnexure \n-\n \nI\n \n \nState wise Farm Production (including In\n-\ncon\nversion) under National Programme of \nOrganic Produce (NPOP) ( in MT)\n \n \nS.\n \nState\n \n2012\n-\n13\n \n2013\n-\n14\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \nNo.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1\n \nAndaman & \nNicobar\n \n0\n \n0\n \n0\n \n0\n \n0\n \n \nIslands\n \n \n \n \n \n \n2\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n5935.626\n \n8361.60\n \n9556.78\n \n6574.311\n \n8372.872\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n3\n \nArunacha\nl Pradesh\n \n60.622\n \n17.34\n \n0\n \n0\n \n37.646\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n4\n \nAssam\n \n4832.723\n \n7923.87\n \n7515.37\n \n9543.558\n \n32395.826